# The shared libraries the AppImage leaves to the machine it runs on
# (PLATFORM-013): linux/appimage/build_appdir.sh neither bundles these nor
# follows what they link. One soname per line, then a tab and why.
#
# The base is the AppImage community's list (pkg2appimage's excludelist at
# master in November 2026): glibc, which the AppImage's floor is (Ubuntu
# 24.04's 2.39), and what the GPU driver or the desktop session must agree on.
ld-linux.so.2	glibc
ld-linux-x86-64.so.2	glibc
ld-linux-aarch64.so.1	glibc
libanl.so.1	glibc
libBrokenLocale.so.1	glibc
libc.so.6	glibc
libdl.so.2	glibc
libm.so.6	glibc
libmvec.so.1	glibc
libnss_compat.so.2	glibc
libnss_dns.so.2	glibc
libnss_files.so.2	glibc
libpthread.so.0	glibc
libresolv.so.2	glibc
librt.so.1	glibc
libthread_db.so.1	glibc
libutil.so.1	glibc
libstdc++.so.6	the GPU driver links the machine's, which is never older than the one built against
libgcc_s.so.1	as libstdc++
libGL.so.1	the GPU driver's
libEGL.so.1	the GPU driver's
libGLESv2.so.2	the GPU driver's
libGLdispatch.so.0	the GPU driver's
libGLX.so.0	the GPU driver's
libOpenGL.so.0	the GPU driver's
libglapi.so.0	the GPU driver's
libgbm.so.1	the GPU driver's
libdrm.so.2	the GPU driver's
libxcb.so.1	the X server's protocol, which the GPU driver links too
libX11.so.6	as libxcb
libX11-xcb.so.1	as libxcb
libxcb-dri2.so.0	the GPU driver's
libxcb-dri3.so.0	the GPU driver's
libwayland-client.so.0	the compositor's protocol, which the GPU driver links too
libwayland-egl.so.1	the GPU driver's
libwayland-cursor.so.0	as libwayland-client
libwayland-server.so.0	libgbm links it
libasound.so.2	the sound server's
libjack.so.0	the sound server's
libpipewire-0.3.so.0	the PipeWire daemon's; its client loads the machine's SPA plugins, built against it
libfontconfig.so.1	reads the machine's font configuration, whose format moves with it
libfreetype.so.6	as fontconfig
libharfbuzz.so.0	as fontconfig
libfribidi.so.0	as fontconfig
libexpat.so.1	the GPU driver links it
libz.so.1	everywhere, and the GPU driver links it
libcom_err.so.2	the machine's Kerberos
libgpg-error.so.0	the machine's
libICE.so.6	the X session's
libSM.so.6	the X session's
libusb-1.0.so.0	the machine's
libuuid.so.1	the machine's
libgmp.so.10	the machine's
#
# Beyond the community's list.
libp11-kit.so.0	GnuTLS finds the trusted certificates through it, at the module paths of the machine's p11-kit; Debian's would look where Fedora and openSUSE keep none
